Publish audit; mark questions APPROVED and answerPending false? Only those with correct answers, which are validated. Set status APPROVED for included questions.

Also groups assignment sync on PATCH: verify all group ids exist, then transaction deleteMany + createMany. If published, changing groups should be allowed? For published quizzes, editing config might invalidate attempts. Better: allow editing config while PUBLISHED only some fields? Simpler: allow edits but block changing questions after attempts? For now Phase 3 can restrict editing after published? Requirement: teacher configures then publishes. Real-world needs edit/closes. Implement: if status CLOSED → no changes (409). If PUBLISHED and has attempts > 0 → block changing questions and availability? That complexity later. For now allow PATCH on PUBLISHED but audit; question changes blocked if attempts exist? Let's enforce: once published, questions cannot be changed (avoid altering in-progress attempts); config can change. On PATCH quiz check if `preguntas` provided and status==='PUBLISHED' && attempts>0 → conflicto. Also if status CLOSED → all edits blocked. Fine.

Groups always sync allowed even published? Could add group mid-quiz; acceptable.

